# aPToP Exercise 137(b) solution — integer swap (exact solution text).

laws boolean
state a, b, c: int

theorem ex137b: (a:= a+b. b:= a–b. a:= a–b) ≡ a′=b ∧ b′=a ∧ c′=c
    a:= a+b. b:= a–b. a:= a–b                    expand last assignment
=   a:= a+b. b:= a–b. a′ = a–b ∧ b′=b ∧ c′=c     Substitution Law
=   a:= a+b. a′ = a–(a–b) ∧ b′ = a–b ∧ c′=c      Substitution Law
=   a′=b ∧ b′ = (a+b)–b ∧ c′=c                   subtract
=   a′=b ∧ b′=a ∧ c′=c
